## reading (stated, not over-claimed)
- volatile: no probe at all (0 store requests); /health/ready p95 0.856ms ≈ /health/live 0.878ms — unchanged behaviour for dev/volatile.
- live-local default cache 1.0s: 15 probes in 15s at 100 rps = exactly 1 probe/s (bounded by the cache + single-flight, independent of the request rate); /health/ready p95 6.3ms / p99 9.6ms (requests landing on a cache miss wait for the probe through the counting proxy); /api/system/status p95 34.8ms alone vs 29.6ms during the flood = no measurable degradation (noise-level).
- live-local cache 0 (worst case, operator-configured): 1396 probes for 1500 requests (93/s; single-flight coalesced ~7%) => the store sees ~1 HEAD per readiness request; /health/ready p95 12.2ms; side endpoint p95 37.5 vs 37.2ms. Recommendation: keep the default; 0 only for debugging.
- /health/live never touches storage (p95 ≤ 1.1ms in every mode).

