## BEFORE vs AFTER (BEFORE = log 368 §fr_storage, same scenario, ca0a7384 code path without SEC-10)
BEFORE: stop rule S3 (p95 censored windows) at 20.0s; detection_latency_s=9.869; ready_statuses_during_outage=['200']
AFTER : stop rule S5 (readiness_failure, 503 'storage timeout') at 11.153s; detection_latency_s=1.005; ready_statuses_during_outage=['503']; post_resume_to_ready_s=0.036; pre-fault tasks lost=0
=> detection 9.87s -> 1.005s (≈ AGOS_READY_STORAGE_TIMEOUT_S 1.0s + probe interval), and readiness now reports the outage the load balancer needs; recovery to 200 in 0.036s after SIGCONT; 0 tasks lost; post-recovery baseline ok.

## not measured here
- hosted Supabase latency/rate limits for the HEAD probe (R-182); multi-instance probe load on a shared store (N instances => N probes/s at the default); a platform load balancer actually acting on /health/ready (Render's health check is still /api/system/status — owner deploy decision).
